15. Traditions of the Holy Prophet also do not lay down any fixed or rigid rule. The Holy Prophet;

(a) decided the case on the evidence of the testimony of a woman plaintiff ;

(b) on the testimony of one female witness ;

(c) on evidence produced by both the parties ;

(d) on the evidence of witness and the oath of the plaintiff ; (e) on the oath of the defendant ; and

(f) on the evidence of two or more witnesses and the oath of the defendant
